Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||11-21-2001||03:14 PM||||Is there any way to adjust (tighten) the rack on my fiero?  I checked the front end out and there seems to be a  little play coming from it.  (by jacking the car up and trying to turn the wheels by hand while someone holds the steering wheel tight)<P>I have another complete tight rack to install, but I dont have the time right now <BR>to install it.<P>I need to take the car in for alignment, would they be able to get an accurate alignment with the play in it? or tighten it while they are at it? <P>When the alignment is out bad (Balljoints,ctrl arm bolts), would that cause the noise on the front end?<P>Thanks<P><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||West Coast Fiero||11-21-2001||04:13 PM||||there is a preload spring in the rack located just above the input shaft. To adjust first remove the hexagon shaped jam nut. once this is removed tighten the preload spring lightly until it bottoms out, them follow that with a 30 degree turn. the jam nut can be removed with a pipe wrench, and the preload spring is 7/8 wrench.<P> while under there remember to check the inner tie rod ends as these are prone to always fail first ( joints located within the rack boots )<P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
